        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Javier Frana, Thomaz Koch, Patricia Tarabini, Sandra Cecchini, Laura Garrone\n- Organizations: ESPN Latin America\n- Events: French Open, Wimbledon, U.S. National Championships, 1995 Styrian Open – Doubles\n- Places: Argentina, Brazil, Porto Alegre\n- Roles: tennis player, tennis commentator\n\nFacts:\n- Thomaz Koch was born on May 11, 1945, in Porto Alegre, Brazil.\n- Thomaz Koch is a left-handed former tennis player from Brazil.\n- Thomaz Koch was a quarter-finalist at the French Open, Wimbledon, and the U.S. National Championships.\n- Javier Frana was born on December 25, 1966.\n- Javier Frana is a former tennis player from Argentina and a current tennis commentator for ESPN Latin America.\n- In 1995, Sandra Cecchini and Patricia Tarabini were the defending champions in the Styrian Open doubles event, but only Cecchini competed that year, partnering with Laura Garrone.\n- In 1996, Patricia Tarabini won the French Open mixed doubles title with Javier Frana.",
